course: dictionary
lesson: 8566
title: Scary: a word for fear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scary means making you feel afraid or frightened. It is an adjective, so it describes a thing or a place, such as a scary film or a scary dark room. Its forms are scary, scarier and scariest.
explain: Read the sentence: «Leaving a group can feel scary, but trusted adults can help.» The word feel tells you scary is about a feeling. Leaving a group might make you frightened, but the sentence shows you that help is there.
explain: Scary can describe stories and films. Monsters, ghosts and dark places are often scary in stories. Halloween is meant to be scary in a fun way. Scary can also describe real life, like the first day at school or going to the dentist.
fact: Scary means making you feel afraid or frightened.
fact: «Scary» is an adjective, so it describes a noun: a scary film, a scary place.
fact: The forms are scary, scarier and scariest.
fact: In stories, scary parts often include monsters, ghosts and dark places.
fact: «A bit scary» is milder than «terrifying».
exercise: «Never go anywhere with someone you don't know, however urgent or scary their story.» What does scary mean here? | *Making you feel afraid or frightened | Making you feel happy and relaxed | Easy to understand | Very loud and noisy
exercise: «Leaving a group can feel scary, but trusted adults can help.» Who can help? | Monsters and ghosts | *Trusted adults, such as parents, teachers and youth workers | Nobody at all | Only the person who is leaving
exercise: «Halloween is meant to be scary in a fun way.» What does this suggest? | *Being frightened in a safe, fun way | Being sad and alone | Being hungry and tired | Being very cold and wet
test: What is the comparative form of scary? | scaryer | *scarier | scarest | more scary-er
test: «A bit scary» is milder than which word? | *terrifying | happy | calm | funny
exam: Scary means making you feel what? | happy and calm | *afraid or frightened | tired | bored
